---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="AudioDrop"
  subtitle="Music applications for desktop and Android, built as separate projects with a shared long-term product direction."
  eyebrow="Open Source"
  stack={['Python', 'PyQt6', 'yt-dlp', 'FFmpeg', 'Kotlin', 'Jetpack Compose', 'Media3']}
>
  <div class="case-grid">
    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Desktop</h2>
      <p>
        AudioDrop Desktop is a Windows music application with local playback, playlists,
        YouTube search, previews, MP3 downloads, playlist downloads, a visualizer and
        dependency management for yt-dlp and FFmpeg.
      </p>
      <p><a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/IgnacioVerde/audiodrop-desktop" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View Desktop repository ↗</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Android</h2>
      <p>
        The Android project is an active work in progress built with Kotlin, Jetpack Compose
        and Media3. Local music playback is functional, while additional features are still
        being implemented.
      </p>
      <p><a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/IgnacioVerde/audiodrop-android" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View Android repository ↗</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>
